6. Covenants
(a) The Borrower covenants and agrees to the following:

    (i) To use the Loan proceeds solely for the Loan Purpose and not for any other purpose.

    (ii) To maintain sufficient liquidity during the Loan Term to meet its obligations under this Agreement.

    (iii) To maintain accurate and complete financial records and to make them available to the Lender upon request.

    (iv) To notify the Lender promptly of any material adverse change in its financial condition, business, or operations.

    (v) To comply with all applicable laws, rules, regulations, orders, judgments, or decrees in connection with the Loan and the Loan Purpose.

(b) The Lender covenants and agrees to the following:

    (i) To provide the Loan proceeds to the Borrower in accordance with the terms of this Agreement.

    (ii) To not unreasonably withhold consent to any proposed action of the Borrower that is consistent with the Loan Purpose and not materially adverse to the Lender's interests.

    (iii) To not accelerate the repayment of the Loan, except in the event of a default under this Agreement.

(c) The parties acknowledge and agree that the covenants set forth in this Section are material to the Lender's decision to enter into this Agreement and to extend credit to the Borrower. The Borrower's breach of any of its covenants under this Section shall constitute an event of default under this Agreement.

7. Interest and Fees
TEXT:
(a) The Borrower shall pay interest on the outstanding principal balance of the Loan at the rate of twelve percent (12%) per annum, calculated on the basis of a 360-day year.

(b) The Lender shall be entitled to charge a processing fee of five percent (5%) of the Loan amount, payable upon the disbursement of the Loan proceeds.

(c) The Borrower shall also be responsible for any and all expenses incurred by the Lender in connection with the Loan, including but not limited to, legal fees, document preparation fees, and other out-of-pocket expenses. These expenses shall be added to the outstanding principal balance of the Loan and shall bear interest at the same rate as the Loan.

(d) The Borrower shall pay all fees and expenses in U.S. dollars.

(e) The Borrower shall make all payments due under this Agreement in accordance with the repayment terms set forth in Section 8 of this Agreement. Any late payment shall accrue interest at the rate of twelve percent (12%) per annum, calculated on the basis of a 360-day year, from the due date until the date of payment.

(f) The Lender may charge a fee for any late payment, which shall be equal to five percent (5%) of the amount of the late payment. This fee shall be payable upon demand.

(g) In the event of any default under this Agreement, the Lender may charge a reasonable attorney's fee and other reasonable costs and expenses incurred in enforcing its rights under this Agreement. These fees and expenses shall be added to the outstanding principal balance of the Loan and shall bear interest at the same rate as the Loan.

8. Loan Term
(a) The term of this Loan shall be five (5) years from the Agreement Date.

(b) The Borrower shall make monthly repayments of the principal and interest for the duration of the Loan term, commencing three (3) months after the Agreement Date.

(c) The maturity date of the Loan shall be the date on which the Borrower makes its final repayment in accordance with the repayment schedule.

9. Default and Remedies
(a) In the event of default by the Borrower under this Agreement, the Lender shall have the right to declare the entire outstanding principal balance of the Loan immediately due and payable.

(b) Upon such declaration, the Borrower shall pay to the Lender all amounts then due and payable under this Agreement, including accrued and unpaid interest, fees, and expenses.

(c) In the event of default, the Lender may exercise any of the following remedies:

    (i) Foreclosure and sale of any collateral pledged by the Borrower to secure the Loan, in accordance with the terms of any security agreement between the parties.

    (ii) Repossession and sale of any collateral, in the event that no security agreement has been executed.

    (iii) Commencement of legal action against the Borrower to recover the outstanding principal balance, accrued interest, fees, and expenses.

(d) The Borrower shall be responsible for all reasonable costs and expenses, including attorney's fees, incurred by the Lender in connection with any remedies exercised under this Section 9.

(e) The Borrower shall not have any right to redeem or reinstate the Loan after default, except as may be expressly provided in this Agreement.

(f) The rights and remedies provided to the Lender under this Section 9 shall be cumulative and not exclusive, and the Lender may pursue any or all of these remedies concurrently or sequentially.

(g) The Lender's rights and remedies under this Section 9 shall survive any termination or expiration of this Agreement.

10. Governing Law
(a) This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of Alexanderborough, Jordan, without giving effect to its conflict of laws provisions.

(b) Any action or proceeding arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be brought exclusively in the courts of Alexanderborough, Jordan, and the parties hereby irrevocably submit to the jurisdiction of such courts.

(c) The parties acknowledge and agree that a judgment in any such action or proceeding shall be conclusive and may be enforced in any court of competent jurisdiction.

(d) The parties shall bear their own costs and expenses in connection with any such action or proceeding, except as otherwise provided in this Agreement.

(e) The failure of any party to assert any right or remedy under this Section 10 shall not constitute a waiver of such right or remedy, and no waiver of any provision of this Section 10 shall be effective unless in writing and signed by the party against whom enforcement of such waiver is sought.

